{"id": "viva_genesis.composites.mixed_amphiphile_protocell.mixed_amphiphile_protocell", "name": "mixed_amphiphile_protocell", "description": "A reusable mixed-amphiphile protocell module (Module G). Coarse-grained vesicle self-assembly + permeability calibrated to Jordan 2019: mixed single-chain amphiphiles broaden the pH / salt / divalent stability window and form vesicles that retain chemistry while staying permeable to the gradient (individuality without isolation). mix_fraction\u22480 / high salt / acidic pH give the controls. Coarse-grained reproduction (not wrapped MD).", "parameters": {"mix_fraction": {"type": "float", "default": 0.4, "description": "Co-surfactant fraction (0 = single fatty acid; higher = broader Jordan window)"}, "pH": {"type": "float", "default": 9.0, "description": "Environment pH (alkaline vent)"}, "ionic_strength": {"type": "float", "default": 0.35, "description": "Ionic strength (M); ~seawater 0.35"}, "temperature": {"type": "float", "default": 318.15, "description": "Temperature (K)"}}, "state": {"membrane": {"_type": "process", "address": "local:ProtocellAssemblyProcess", "config": {"mix_fraction": 0.4}, "interval": 1.0, "inputs": {"pH": ["env", "pH"], "ionic_strength": ["env", "ionic_strength"], "temperature": ["env", "temperature"], "mix_fraction": ["env", "mix_fraction"]}, "outputs": {"membrane_area": ["protocell", "membrane_area"], "permeability": ["protocell", "permeability"], "compartment_volume": ["protocell", "compartment_volume"], "viable_compartments": ["protocell", "viable_compartments"], "retention": ["protocell", "retention"], "access": ["protocell", "access"], "individuality_access": ["protocell", "individuality_access"]}, "doc": "Coarse-grained physico-chemical model of mixed single-chain amphiphile\nvesicle self-assembly + permeability, calibrated to Jordan 2019. Reads the\nenvironment (pH, ionic strength, temperature); decides vesicle viability from\nthe pH window + salt/divalent tolerance (broadened by the co-surfactant\nfraction); and emits the membrane area, permeability, compartment volume,\nviable-compartment count, and the retention / access / individuality-access\ntradeoff. A reproduction, not a wrapped MD engine \u2014 labeled as such.", "interval_label": "1 s", "_contract": {"summary": "Coarse-grained mixed-amphiphile vesicle self-assembly + permeability, calibrated to Jordan 2019: the individuality-vs-access tradeoff (retain chemistry while staying permeable to the gradient).", "description": "Clean-room reproduction of the Jordan-2019 vesicle-stability physical chemistry (NOT a wrapped MD engine; the proposed primary method is coarse-grained membrane kinetics). Vesicles are viable when pH lies in a band around the bilayer apparent pKa AND ionic strength / divalent cations stay below a tolerance that the co-surfactant fraction broadens; permeability follows a solubility-diffusion Arrhenius law; retention = exp(-P*A/V*tau) and access = P*A*gradient trade off, their product non-empty only in an intermediate window. Favorable (mixed amphiphiles, alkaline, seawater salt) forms viable compartments with retention AND access; a single-fatty-acid control fails on salt tolerance.", "inputs": {"pH": "environment pH (dimensionless)", "ionic_strength": "ionic strength (molar)", "temperature": "temperature (K)"}, "outputs": {"membrane_area": "total vesicle membrane area (meter**2)", "permeability": "membrane solute permeability coefficient (meter/second)", "compartment_volume": "total enclosed compartment volume (liter)", "viable_compartments": "number of viable vesicles (integer)", "retention": "fraction of internal chemistry retained (dimensionless, 0-1)", "access": "external-gradient access / resource import (dimensionless, 0-1)", "individuality_access": "retention x access \u2014 individuality without isolation (dimensionless)"}, "config": {}, "math": ["viable = (|pH - pKa_eff| < window_eff) and (I < I_max_eff) and (Mg < Mg_max_eff) and (T in range)", "P = P0 * exp(-Ea/(R*T)) * (1 + k_P * mix_fraction)", "retention = exp(-P*A/V*tau);  access = tanh(P*A*gradient_scale);  individuality_access = retention*access"], "symbols": {"pKa_eff": "bilayer apparent pKa (shifted up from solution)", "window_eff": "pH half-window (broadened by mix)", "I_max_eff": "ionic-strength tolerance (broadened by mix)", "mix_fraction": "co-surfactant fraction (0 = single fatty acid)"}, "assumptions": ["Coarse-grained reproduction calibrated to Jordan 2019; full membrane MD is out of environment.", "Vesicle viability: pH in [pKa_eff +/- window] AND ionic_strength < I_max AND divalent < Mg_max AND T in range.", "Co-surfactant fraction broadens the pH / salt / divalent tolerance (the Jordan mixed-amphiphile result).", "Permeability: solubility-diffusion Arrhenius in T + composition; retention/access from P*A/V."], "references": ["jordan2019promotion", "sutherland2017opinion"], "face": {"inputs": {}, "outputs": {}}, "amendments": [], "math_mathml": ["<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"block\"><mrow><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>a</mi><mi>b</mi><mi>l</mi><mi>e</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x0007C;</mo><mi>p</mi><mi>H</mi><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mi>p</mi><mi>K</mi><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>e</mi></msub><mi>f</mi><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x0007C;</mo><mo>&#x0003C;</mo><mi>w</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>n</mi><mi>d</mi><mi>o</mi><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>e</mi></msub><mi>f</mi><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mi>I</mi><mo>&#x0003C;</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mi>a</mi><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>e</mi></msub><mi>f</mi><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mi>M</mi><mi>g</mi><mo>&#x0003C;</mo><mi>M</mi><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mi>a</mi><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>e</mi></msub><mi>f</mi><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mi>T</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>n</mi><mi>r</mi><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi><mi>g</mi><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo></mrow></math>", "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"block\"><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mi>P</mi><mn>0</mn><mo>&#x0002A;</mo><mi>e</mi><mi>x</mi><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mi>E</mi><mi>a</mi><mo>&#x0002F;</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mi>R</mi><mo>&#x0002A;</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mo>&#x0002A;</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mo>&#x0002A;</mo><mi>m</mi><mi>i</mi><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mi>r</mi><mi>a</mi><mi>c</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>o</mi><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo></mrow></math>", "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"block\"><mrow><mi>r</mi><mi>e</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>e</mi><mi>n</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>o</mi><mi>n</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mi>e</mi><mi>x</mi><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mi>P</mi><mo>&#x0002A;</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>&#x0002F;</mo><mi>V</mi><mo>&#x0002A;</mo><mi>t</mi><mi>a</mi><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mi>;</mi><mi>a</mi><mi>c</mi><mi>c</mi><mi>e</mi><mi>s</mi><mi>s</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mi>t</mi><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mi>P</mi><mo>&#x0002A;</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>&#x0002A;</mo><mi>g</mi><mi>r</mi><mi>a</mi><mi>d</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>e</mi><mi>n</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mi>c</mi><mi>a</mi><mi>l</mi><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mi>;</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>n</mi><mi>d</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>d</mi><mi>u</mi><mi>a</mi><mi>l</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>t</mi><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mi>c</mi><mi>c</mi><mi>e</mi><mi>s</mi><mi>s</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mi>r</mi><mi>e</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>e</mi><mi>n</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>o</mi><mi>n</mi><mo>&#x0002A;</mo><mi>a</mi><mi>c</mi><mi>c</mi><mi>e</mi><mi>s</mi><mi>s</mi></mrow></math>"]}, "_inputs": {"pH": {"_type": "float", "_units": "dimensionless"}, "ionic_strength": {"_type": "float", "_units": "molar"}, "temperature": {"_type": "float", "_units": "kelvin"}, "mix_fraction": {"_type": "float", "_units": "dimensionless"}}, "_outputs": {"membrane_area": {"_type": "overwrite[float]", "_units": "meter**2"}, "permeability": {"_type": "overwrite[float]", "_units": "meter/second"}, "compartment_volume": {"_type": "overwrite[float]", "_units": "liter"}, "viable_compartments": {"_type": "overwrite[integer]", "_units": "dimensionless"}, "retention": {"_type": "overwrite[float]", "_units": "dimensionless"}, "access": {"_type": "overwrite[float]", "_units": "dimensionless"}, "individuality_access": {"_type": "overwrite[float]", "_units": "dimensionless"}}}, "env": {"pH": 9.0, "ionic_strength": 0.35, "temperature": 318.15, "mix_fraction": 0.4}, "protocell": {"membrane_area": 0.0, "permeability": 0.0, "compartment_volume": 0.0, "viable_compartments": 0, "retention": 0.0, "access": 0.0, "individuality_access": 0.0}, "emitter": {"_type": "step", "address": "local:RAMEmitter", "config": {"emit": {"viable_compartments": "integer", "individuality_access": "float", "retention": "float", "access": "float", "membrane_area": "float", "permeability": "float", "compartment_volume": "float", "global_time": "float"}}, "inputs": {"viable_compartments": ["protocell", "viable_compartments"], "individuality_access": ["protocell", "individuality_access"], "retention": ["protocell", "retention"], "access": ["protocell", "access"], "membrane_area": ["protocell", "membrane_area"], "permeability": ["protocell", "permeability"], "compartment_volume": ["protocell", "compartment_volume"], "global_time": ["global_time"]}, "doc": "Store historical states in memory.\n\n``subsample`` records only every Nth composite tick (default 1 =\nevery tick). Use this for long runs or composites with heavy\nstate (large fields, many agents) to keep RAM bounded \u2014 the\nsaved time-series still reflects the simulation's true cadence\nvia each row's ``global_time`` field.\n\n``max_len`` optionally bounds ``history`` to the most recent N\nrecorded rows (a ring buffer): once the cap is reached each new\nrecord drops the oldest. Default ``None`` = unbounded (the\nhistorical behaviour \u2014 consumers such as v2ecoli that read the\nfull ``history`` are unaffected unless they opt in). ``max_len``\ncounts *recorded* rows (i.e. post-``subsample``).", "_contract": {"summary": "type(object) -> the object's type", "description": "type(name, bases, dict, **kwds) -> a new type", "inputs": {}, "outputs": {}, "config": {}, "math": [], "symbols": {}, "assumptions": [], "references": [], "face": {"inputs": {}, "outputs": {}}, "amendments": []}, "_inputs": {"viable_compartments": "integer", "individuality_access": "float", "retention": "float", "access": "float", "membrane_area": "float", "permeability": "float", "compartment_volume": "float", "global_time": "float"}, "_outputs": {"results": "node"}}, "_declared_emit_paths": ["protocell/viable_compartments", "protocell/individuality_access", "protocell/retention", "protocell/access", "protocell/membrane_area", "protocell/permeability", "protocell/compartment_volume", "global_time"]}, "schema": {}, "overrides": {}, "requires": {}, "tags": [], "visualizations": [{"name": "protocell-window", "address": "local:ProtocellWindowViz", "config": {"title": "The protocell window broadens (mixed amphiphiles)"}}], "analyses": [], "emitters": [{"address": "local:ParquetEmitter", "paths": ["protocell/viable_compartments", "protocell/individuality_access", "protocell/retention", "protocell/access", "protocell/membrane_area", "protocell/permeability", "protocell/compartment_volume", "global_time"]}], "kind": "generator", "module": "viva_genesis.composites.mixed_amphiphile_protocell", "default_n_steps": 20, "preferred_time": "6 hours", "svg": null, "wiring_status": "ready", "run_kind": "temporal", "notice": null}